--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAV REGISTRATION (web route (unrouted))
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web source is an UNROUTED card rendered inside the automations LIST page (a separate parity unit;
the `.automations` AppRoute is that list, NOT this card). Per the prompt ("map (unrouted) to a deep
link / NavigationDestination") the card is registered as a VALUE-based destination, not a new sidebar
AppRoute: `AutomationCardRoute` (Hashable + Codable, carries `automationID`) + a
`View.automationCardDestination()` modifier wiring `.navigationDestination(for: AutomationCardRoute.self)`.
It is attached ONCE on the shell's `RouteHost` (Sources/App/AppShell.swift), which lives inside every
NavigationStack (macOS/iPad split detail, iPhone tabs + More), so any
`NavigationLink(value: AutomationCardRoute(automationID:))` pushes the card detail. The default resolver
seeds a representative automation (mirroring the sibling Tesla Orders route's in-memory seed); production
composition injects the P1/S8 automations holder over the KMP core.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@Observable BINDING (covenant #2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`@MainActor @Observable AutomationCardModel` owns the typed `AutomationCardState` + live
`AutomationLiveConnection`, exposes the page's `load()` / `refresh()` async methods, and projects the
web card's four callbacks (+ the inert Duplicate/Export and the embedded PinButton) into
`AutomationCardActions` that mutate its own in-memory copy — faithful to the web component, which holds
the row locally and never refetches inside the card. No networking/business logic in the view body
(ADR-002): the page (Sources/Features/Automations/AutomationCardPage.swift) is a ScrollView that hosts
`AutomationCard(state:connection:actions:localize:)` and drives it from the model via `.task`/`.refreshable`.

